255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 84 0 R/T(Key Questions & Technical Analysis )/E(Key Questions & Technical Analysis )/Pg 19 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

256 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 84 0 R/T(Q1: What is the difference between the initial bundle and a lazy-loaded chunk in terms of when each is downloaded? )/E(Q1: What is the difference between the initial bundle and a lazy-loaded chunk in terms of when each is downloaded? )/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

257 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Answer: The initial bundle \(index-BUzia4Kc.js\) is requested synchronously on the critical rendering path when the application URL is first loaded into the browser. It contains only the core shell, routing logic, and global design system. Lazy-loaded chunks \(Projects.js, Contact.js, Analytics.js\) are downloaded asynchronously via dynamic import\(\) calls only when the user explicitly navigates to those respective routes. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

258 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 84 0 R/T(Q2: Why does lazy loading improve perceived performance even though the total amount of code downloaded eventually stays the same? )/E(Q2: Why does lazy loading improve perceived performance even though the total amount of code downloaded eventually stays the same? )/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

259 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Answer: Perceived performance is heavily dictated by First Contentful Paint \(FCP\) and Time to Interactive \(TTI\). Smaller initial bundles parse significantly faster in the V8 engine, rendering the interactive UI shell immediately. Furthermore, users often perform tasks without visiting secondary routes like Contact or Analytics; for those users, deferred code is never downloaded at all, saving substantial mobile bandwidth and device memory. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

260 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 84 0 R/T(Q3: In what situations would lazy loading not be worth the added complexity? )/E(Q3: In what situations would lazy loading not be worth the added complexity? )/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

261 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Answer: Lazy loading introduces additional HTTP round-trips and requires Suspense boundary management. In lightweight applications where the entire bundle is under 50\20570 kB, the network latency of separate chunk requests exceeds the negligible parsing savings. Additionally, universally shared utilities \(such as date formatters and core API clients\) should not be split into micro-chunks to avoid excessive waterfall requests. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

